{"id": "EUVD-2026-93182", "enisaUuid": "29dfb7cb-f73d-3bb3-b05a-f3e956e8c5ed", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nswiotlb: use the adjusted address for the highmem page lookup\n\nswiotlb_bounce() reads the page frame number from the slot's recorded\norig_addr, then advances orig_addr by tlb_offset to reach the address\nthe caller asked about. The highmem branch mixes the two: the offset\nwithin the page comes from the adjusted address, the page from the value\nbefore it.\n\nOnce the adjustment crosses a page boundary the pair no longer describes\none location, and the whole copy lands one page below the intended one\nfor a positive tlb_offset, one above for a negative one. DMA_FROM_DEVICE\nwrites the device data over the wrong page and leaves the intended one\nstale, DMA_TO_DEVICE feeds the device from a page the mapping may not\ncover. Partial syncs through dma_sync_single_range_for_*() are what make\ntlb_offset non-zero.\n\nThe branch test is picked the same way, so a slot recorded in lowmem can\nbe adjusted into highmem and the lowmem path then hands a highmem\naddress to phys_to_virt().\n\nTake both from orig_addr once it is final and keep pfn in the branch\nthat uses it. PhysHighMem() asks the question straight from the address,\nas dma-debug already does.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:16:25", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e53b4d6afbde626255805d438cabb1cac482445", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aa4709813b29db89f2307f968db5d24925dcdeb1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0219b72f5c209732b2f03a8cc0d7240b5e428a99", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b7d7914a9ae3097e63d113007e4fb44d33d515b1"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98254", "GHSA-hrh5-h3h2-8q3j"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05b2f7f0-6eb1-3416-a639-a238cf9aba2e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e6108147dd91b94d1979b110f265710c254c99d5"}, {"id": "1f5f6bad-e0c7-3092-911d-894a0601212c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5f89468e2f060031cd89fd4287298e0eaf246bf6 <0219b72f5c209732b2f03a8cc0d7240b5e428a99"}, {"id": "1f9bf01d-863d-3bd5-bbe8-9f5de36dd90a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.13"}, {"id": "4334e038-0b9a-3212-bf1b-5936011fe6c2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "5134cdbd-da97-3388-aa45-009549fe2792", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e77b796eb9b7ca3c1c0d574d0c155f55b59ca8d5"}, {"id": "6d28ed65-94af-35f6-ba96-92f34792b111", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5f89468e2f060031cd89fd4287298e0eaf246bf6 <aa4709813b29db89f2307f968db5d24925dcdeb1"}, {"id": "8623a439-def2-3f54-99b3-7709584afa8a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.12.14 <5.13"}, {"id": "9147976a-1a9b-38d3-b69b-19f298c05a6b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5f89468e2f060031cd89fd4287298e0eaf246bf6 <6e53b4d6afbde626255805d438cabb1cac482445"}, {"id": "91c97bce-0940-3149-8241-1d61f5e866c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a0c92383-cf98-378d-8659-6d201b5cfd4c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "c2d5c87f-d273-3095-8b43-e763bf1188e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "c5825113-228b-3d45-9e09-8a0d34add74c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5f89468e2f060031cd89fd4287298e0eaf246bf6 <b7d7914a9ae3097e63d113007e4fb44d33d515b1"}, {"id": "dfc26779-